${HARDENING_BLOCK}
!
${BREAKGLASS_BLOCK}
!
! --- Step 1: RADIUS server, group and AAA (the standard block, where RADIUS has it) ---
! The order keeps the session you paste from alive: 'aaa new-model' first (nothing under 'aaa'
! exists on IOS until it is set), then the server and its group, the login lists and exec
! authorization. RADIUS has no command authorization. From 'aaa new-model' until the login lists
! are typed a NEW RADIUS login would fail (a local user still gets in): paste the block in one go
! and keep the session you paste from.
! Encrypt Type 0 plaintext secrets in running-config.
! (Type 7 is trivially reversible; for Type 6 AES encryption of the
!  RADIUS key, run 'key config-key password-encrypt <master>' first,
!  then re-enter the key with 'key 6 <encrypted-string>'.)
service password-encryption
!
aaa new-model
!
radius server RADIUS
  address ipv4 ${SERVER_IP} auth-port ${AUTH_PORT} acct-port ${ACCT_PORT}
  key ${SECRET}
  timeout 5
  retransmit 2
!
aaa group server radius ${RADIUS_GROUP}
  server name RADIUS
!
${SOURCE_INTERFACE_BLOCK}
!
! 'default' is the vty lines' login list; CONSOLE is the console's, local only: with the
! server up a local user logs in on the console, and lands at privilege 1 (see Notes below).
aaa authentication login default ${AUTHN_METHODS}
aaa authentication login CONSOLE local
aaa authorization exec default ${AUTHZ_EXEC_METHODS}
! 'enable' against a RADIUS server is NOT VERIFIED (lab item E2): IOS sends the user enab15 and
! what your server answers is unknown. With a reachable server that does not answer enable
! requests positively, 'enable' FAILS; the local enable secret is used only when no server
! answers. Left commented on purpose: type it only after 'enable' is shown to work.
! aaa authentication enable default group ${RADIUS_GROUP} enable
aaa accounting exec default start-stop group ${RADIUS_GROUP}
aaa session-id common
!
${PRIVILEGE_COMMANDS}
${SNMP_BLOCK}
!
${VTY_ACL_BLOCK}
!
${NETCONF_BLOCK}
!
line con 0
  login authentication CONSOLE
  exec-timeout ${EXEC_TIMEOUT} 0
!
line vty 0 15
  login authentication default
  transport input ssh
${VTY_ACCESS_CLASS}
  exec-timeout ${EXEC_TIMEOUT} 0
